      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While you are busy, you must monitor the wound closely for signs of infection, which is the biggest danger. Look out for increasing redness spreading away from the puncture site, warmth, swelling, throbbing pain, or the presence of pus. If you notice any of these signs, or if your fever spikes, seek immediate medical attention without delay. Do not wait several days if you begin to feel unwell.",
      "source": "target",
